{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_8_security_27_audit_logging_page", "label": "Audit logging and tamper-evidence", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-8-security/27-audit-logging.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Who did what to which record, when, and did it work. When Needed \u2014 privileged actions, regulated data, multi-tenant."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_8_security_27_audit_logging_audit_event", "label": "Audit event schema", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-8-security/27-audit-logging.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Actor+type, closed action vocabulary, target type+id, before/after, outcome including denials, requestId. Write next to the update, not in the controller."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_8_security_27_audit_logging_hash_chain", "label": "HMAC hash chain", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-8-security/27-audit-logging.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each record HMACs canonical({payload, seq, prev}). Unkeyed sha256 lets an editor recompute the chain. Canonical key order is required."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_8_security_27_audit_logging_truncation_blindness", "label": "Hash-chain truncation blindness", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-8-security/27-audit-logging.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deleting from the end leaves a shorter valid chain. Publish the head MAC to a system the app cannot rewrite; the anchoring period is the attacker window."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_8_security_27_audit_logging_append_only_storage", "label": "Append-only is a